  "limits": [
    "Twenty-four native cases run both stack-copy modes on controlled partial four-player boards. Twelve packaged witnesses run actual native payments and bounded phases without response priority.",
    "The equipment-leaves case uses Disperse on a legal nonland permanent; equipped-creature bounce uses Unsummon. Both check native target admission.",
    "Attachment IDs, canonical mapped targets in native tests and command-zone effect counts are checked. Reattaching creates one new effect after removing the old effect.",
    "Land sources are installed on the battlefield. Spells and activation costs are paid natively. Generator Servant waits a full turn cycle before tapping; sacrifice, Arena exertion and Hall life costs are observed.",
    "Haste is checked before and after deadlines, with actual spent-mana source IDs; general attack admission, multiple-spell allocation and all copied mana-source abilities remain unverified.",
    "Only the selected Reconfigure cards and paths are exercised; other card abilities, ordinary equipment, living weapon, all attachment restrictions and overlapping keyword grants need separate validation.",
    "Banishing Light host-bound exile return currently fails in both snapshot modes in a separate research probe; original-game paid returns pass. This milestone does not fix it.",
    "Other callbacks, hidden/merged/perpetual state, arbitrary continuations and general AI policy remain incomplete. Unmapped diagnostics are asserted in these fixtures, not aggregated into normal simulation reports.",
    "Catalog construction proves script availability, not full gameplay correctness. Seven unavailable entries are nonstarting meld results. The retained rules reference is versioned rather than a complete current-rules audit."
  ]
